WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:08.385
In this video, you will record a local business that paid you to sponsor your contest, so its name and logo are thanked on your contest page.

00:00:08.385 --> 00:00:09.509
We start on the map.

00:00:10.409 --> 00:00:14.471
To begin, open your web browser, and go to SoCal Lights dot app.

00:00:14.471 --> 00:00:16.596
That is the only address you need.

00:00:19.427 --> 00:00:21.834
This is the SoCal Lights home page.

00:00:21.834 --> 00:00:25.578
The first time you visit, it asks to use your location.

00:00:25.578 --> 00:00:26.915
Tap Use my location.

00:00:28.669 --> 00:00:33.106
That is how the map shows how far things are, and gives you directions.

00:00:33.106 --> 00:00:36.311
Your browser asks permission as well, so tap Allow.

00:00:36.311 --> 00:00:40.872
Your location is used only on your device, and you can say no at any time.

00:00:44.353 --> 00:00:47.042
Now look at the top right corner of the map.

00:00:47.042 --> 00:00:48.237
See the three dots?

00:00:48.237 --> 00:00:52.540
That is the menu, and it is the doorway to everything else on the site.

00:00:52.540 --> 00:00:53.078
Tap them.

00:00:54.679 --> 00:00:56.317
In the menu, tap Contests.

00:00:56.317 --> 00:01:01.655
That is where every neighborhood contest lives: the ones you can vote in, enter, or run.

00:01:03.343 --> 00:01:03.925
Tap Mine.

00:01:03.925 --> 00:01:05.556
This is your personal page.

00:01:05.556 --> 00:01:10.916
It lists the contests you run, if you run any, and the homes you entered, with their status.

00:01:12.591 --> 00:01:14.637
Tap Manage, next to your contest.

00:01:14.637 --> 00:01:18.309
This opens your dashboard, the control room for your contest.

00:01:20.193 --> 00:01:23.846
A sponsor is a local business that supports your contest.

00:01:23.846 --> 00:01:25.987
This tab is where you record one.

00:01:25.987 --> 00:01:26.806
Tap Sponsors.

00:01:28.588 --> 00:01:30.464
Type the company's name.

00:01:30.464 --> 00:01:36.545
Then choose their logo, a J P G, P N G, or WebP file under six hundred kilobytes.

00:01:38.818 --> 00:01:40.671
Now how the sponsorship counts.

00:01:40.671 --> 00:01:43.682
The sponsor paid you yourself, so choose Paid to me.

00:01:44.584 --> 00:01:48.927
Tick that you collected the payment, and add the date and how it was paid.

00:01:48.927 --> 00:01:51.069
Sponsors pay you, never SoCal Lights.

00:01:53.643 --> 00:01:57.781
Tick that you have the sponsor's permission, and tick Show on the contest page.

00:02:00.119 --> 00:02:01.247
Tap Save sponsor.

00:02:01.247 --> 00:02:03.191
Payment never affects who wins.

00:02:05.116 --> 00:02:12.028
To check how it looks, tap See it as voters do, and you will see the sponsor on the contest page, just as your neighbors do.

00:02:14.007 --> 00:02:16.589
Next up: Invite a sponsor to your contest.
